{"id":"000W0A","title":"Kroopki Chaos (6x6)","author":"Oddlyeven","solvedCount":5,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-12T03:52:06+00:00","posted":"Heute, 01:09 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle is part of the puzzle pack Chaotic Construction by the Sudoku Skunkworks. Please check it out!\nRules:\n\nChaos Construction: Divide the grid into regions of 6 orthogonally connected cells each, such that every cell is part of exactly one region. Place the digits 1 to 6 exactly once in each row, column and region.\n\nKroopki doots: Doots are thick lines between sets of cells. A white doot separates two sets of cells whose respective sums are consecutive. A black doot separates two sets of cells whose respective sums are in a 1:2 ratio. Doots also act as region borders.\n\nSight circles: Digits in circles indicate the number of cells seen horizontally and vertically within the same region, including itself. Cells from other regions block vision.\n\nExample grid (not intended to be solvable):\n\nSudokuPad - Penpa+","solutionCode":"Row 4, left to right, with a - for each internal region border.","tags":["Sudoku","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/0240wx9kes","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/3x2ed7ex","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/0240wx9kes","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":6,"cols":6,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-12T03:52:06+00:00"}